DS OST on 13th Oct 2026-B2 Batch
by Prof. Shweta Chachra - Tuesday, 29 September 2026, 11:54 AM
---------------------------------------------------------------------
Dear Students,

The=C2=A0 B2 Batch DS Lab OST is scheduled on 13th Oct 2026 during the regu=
lar
lab timings i.e. 9-11am.

Kindly come prepared for the same.

Syllabus -Exp 1-6.

Kindly refer to the mail by Prof. Swati Mali ma'am=C2=A0 regarding OST for
further details.

Note: Variations and concepts related to the experiment list can be asked
for practical implementation.
Practical Examination Total Marks - 25 Marks (Refer tables below for
distribution of marks)

Time Duration: Strictly 2 hrs=C2=A0

=C2=A0Change of Experiment: - 3 marks

=C2=A0

Important:

*
Carrying any study material/electronic gadgets will be considered unfair
means.

*
Any indiscipline during the examination will be considered as unfair means

*
All unfair means cases will be reported to COE.

Other instructions:

*
Students will choose a question sheet for them.

*
Each sheet will have only one question.

*
Students should follow the =E2=80=9Cquestion content=E2=80=9D exactly (data=
 structure
mentioned, memory allocation policy, outputs expected etc).

*
Students can use the question sheet for rough work. On request, an extra
sheet can be provided if needed.

*
They might have to explain the code when asked by teachers.

*
Students will have to report in time and complete the
execution+modification within the stipulated time of 2 hrs

*
The batches may have different sets of experiments for OST exams.

Weightage Breakdown (Total: 25 Marks)

Evaluation Parameter

Marks

Weightage

Core Focus Area

1. Logic Explanation & On-Screen Modification

10

40%

Line-by-line walkthrough, conceptual defense, execution state after live
modification

2. Execution & Testing

8

32%

Base code compilation, standard test cases, boundary/edge case validation

3. Code Quality

7

28%

Modular layout, pointer integrity, dynamic memory management (free/delete)

Thankyou,

